          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಕಾನೂನು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕಾನೂನು — kānūnu — \"a law; the law\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಈ ಕಾನೂನು ಮುಂದಿನ ತಿಂಗಳಿನಿಂದ ಬರುತ್ತದೆ. ī kānūnu mundina tiṅgaḷininda baruttade. This law comes in from next month."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕಾನೂನುಬದ್ಧ, legal; ಕಾನೂನುಬಾಹಿರ, illegal."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕಾನೂನು (kānūnu) is a loan from Arabic qānūn, \"a rule, a canon\", through Persian and Hindustani; Arabic took it from Greek kanōn, \"a rule\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
          ]
        },
